=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client data port, also Microsoft.UI-free),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view).
  Mirrors the sibling BatteryDegradationPage / ChargingCurvePage surfaces.
- Data sources — the web page's two hooks, each ported to the generated OpenAPI client (ADR-004):
  * useRegenEfficiency → GET /analytics/regen [start,end] (operation get_api_v1_analytics_regen): the PRIMARY
    read; its presence gates the page success/empty branch and its failure surfaces the page error, exactly as
    the web page gates on `data ?`. Parsed into RegenSummary (Model.cs RegenSummary.FromJson; total_regen_wh /
    total_drive_wh / regen_ratio / monthly_avg_regen / free_charges, snake_case with camelCase alias, ?? 0).
  * useDrives → GET /drives (operation get_api_v1_drives): the SECONDARY best-effort read that feeds the
    client-side monthly-trend chart + the recent-drives table; a transport failure degrades to no drives
    (RegenEfficiencyClientFeed.FetchDrivesAsync catches ApiException → empty), mirroring the web's two
    independent queries. Parsed by RegenEfficiencyClientFeed.ParseDrives → RegenDrive.FromJson.
- Projection (RegenEfficiencyProjection.Project) is the 1:1 port of the web render body + its regenColor /
  getRegenRatio / monthlyTrend / regenDrives helpers. State precedence mirrors the web data lifecycle
  (loading → error → empty → success). The backend rollup feeds the hero gauge, the six stat cards and the
  four metric bars; the drive list feeds the monthly-trend composed chart (bucket by yyyy-MM, sum regen Wh /
  count / sum distance, most-recent 12, regenKwh = Wh/1000, distance via the user unit) and the recent-drives
  table (regen-positive drives, ≤20, per-drive ratio = regenEnergyWh/energyUsedWh*100 guarded by avgPowerW>0).
- Units (P1/S5): energy is SI watt-hours, power SI watts, distance SI meters on the wire; every readout is
  converted only at the projection boundary via UnitFormatters.FormatEnergy/FormatPower +
  UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi + ScalarFormatters (percent/number). Nothing non-SI is stored or computed. The
  regen.recoveredInfo "{0} kWh" line restates Wh→kWh at the boundary (the kWh unit is intrinsic to the catalog
  template, matching the web formatEnergy(...) string).
- Nav: route name RegenEfficiency → path regen-efficiency already exists in RouteTable.cs#282; the page factory
  is registered in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs ("RegenEfficiency" → new FeatureViews.Driving.RegenEfficiencyPage()).
- Catalog: 29 of the 30 web i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw
  (translation.* prefix); the one missing key, regen.monthlyTrend.aria, was added to all three locales
  ("Monthly regen energy and drive count composed chart"). No other catalog rows added; every visible literal
  resolves through ILocalizer with the web key names.

